        "content": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n  <title>Variant component</title>\n\n  <!-- Tailwind is loaded per the required approach, but the source page ships\n       zero CSS of its own -- it renders with the browser's plain default\n       (User-Agent) stylesheet: serif body copy, default h1/p margins, and\n       broken-image placeholders for the (non-existent) product photos.\n       Preflight is disabled so those un-styled defaults are preserved\n       exactly instead of being normalized away by Tailwind's reset. -->\n  <script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>\n  <script>\n    tailwind.config = {\n      corePlugins: {\n        preflight: false\n      }\n    };\n  </script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <main id=\"main\">\n    <h1>Shop</h1>\n\n    <!-- Reusable \"product-card\" component: image + name/price line, with an\n         optional \"badge\" component (a small \"Featured\" label) for items\n         that are on sale/highlighted. Neither class carries any CSS in the\n         source, so no visual card/grid treatment is invented here -- the\n         class names are kept as the semantic hooks the source markup used. -->\n    <div class=\"product-card\">\n      <img src=\"/product-1.jpg\" alt=\"Trail Runner Jacket\" />\n      <p>Trail Runner Jacket — $128</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"product-card\">\n      <span class=\"badge\">Featured</span>\n      <img src=\"/product-2.jpg\" alt=\"Insulated Bottle\" />\n      <p>Insulated Bottle — $32</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"product-card\">\n      <img src=\"/product-3.jpg\" alt=\"Camp Lantern\" />\n      <p>Camp Lantern — $45</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"product-card\">\n      <span class=\"badge\">Featured</span>\n      <img src=\"/product-4.jpg\" alt=\"Rain Shell\" />\n      <p>Rain Shell — $96</p>\n    </div>\n  </main>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
